    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 39 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did to consolidate duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`:\n\n**1. `Owner.java` \u2014 added the derived key**\n```java\npublic String getIdentityKey() {\n    String telephonePart = this.telephone == null ? \"\" : this.telephone;\n    String emailPart = this.email == null ? \"\" : this.email;\n    String householdPart = this.householdId == null ? \"\" : this.householdId;\n    return telephonePart + \"|\" + emailPart + \"|\" + householdPart;\n}\n```\nIt's built from the already-normalized stored telephone (E.164) and email (lower-cased), with a missing email or household id rendered as empty \u2014 matching the format the tests assert (`telephone||householdId` when email is absent).\n\n**2. `openapi.yml` \u2014 exposed `identityKey`** as a read-only field on the `Owner` schema, so it's regenerated into `OwnerDto` and returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` (MapStruct maps it automatically like the other derived getters).\n\n**3. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` \u2014 replaced three separate checks with one:**\n- Removed the standalone email-in-use `CONFLICT`.\n- Removed the standalone telephone-in-use `CONFLICT`.\n- Removed the \"same household but not `sharesHousehold`\" `CONFLICT`; the household-grouping logic (assigning/back-filling `householdId` and `householdSize`) stays.\n- Added a single check that rejects with 409 only when the new owner's whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's.\n\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, household members with different telephones now get distinct identity keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The unrelated city-capacity 409 (a quota, not duplicate detection) is untouched, so Cp18 still passes, and the identity tests (Cp03/Cp10/Cp11/Cp25/Cp28) all pass under the new key.",
